  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Find the shortest distance between the point $(4,3)$ and the line $x=2.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934287/assets/ea64c0752738b0c917d897060351cdd43ed7bbf687cc20781b7241ee3be0ad3c.png)\n\nSince the line $x=2$ is a vertical line, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(4,3)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between the $x$-coordinate of the point and $2.$ \n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=|4-2|=2.\n$$",
